      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_shifted: insert_after_residue 32 -> 27 on human canonical P31431 (paper numbering: ortholog:rat, construct species: rat). Paper (PMID 26068620): \"Syndecan-4-HA: The HA-tag was fused into the extracellular domain after aa 32, and was a gift from John Couchman, University of Copenhagen, Denmark [ 16 ].\". Audit note: Species is not stated in this paper; the source paper (ref 16, Gopal et al. 2010 JBC, PMC2863221) describes rat syndecan-4 with HA 'between isoleucine 32 and aspartate 33'. Rat ETEVI|DPQDL maps to human I27|D28 (rat signal peptide is 5 aa longer), so human insert_after = 27; human 32|33 is L|L, 5 residues downstream. Surface: immuno-EM gold at the plasma membrane here, live-cell anti-HA in Gopal 2010.] L2 explicitly states the HA-tag is fused after amino acid 32 in the extracellular domain of full-length SDC4. Position 32 (L) and 33 (L) are within the extracellular domain (19-149), 14 residues into the ectodomain, and 117 residues from the TM boundary. L4 (same paper) confirms plasma membrane localization by immuno-EM. Python confirms residue_before=L, residue_after=L. Full-length SDC4 construct with HA-tag fused into the extracellular domain after amino acid 32, gifted from John Couchman (University of Copenhagen); plasma membrane localization confirmed by immuno-EM in bovine muscle cells.",
