      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "L5 and L7 (PMC13050698) describe an HA-tagged SDC4 with the tag at the N-terminus of the extracellular domain, but no specific residue is named. SDC4 has a signal peptide spanning residues 1-18 and a single extracellular N-terminus beginning at residue 19; the tag must therefore follow the signal peptide cleavage site (after residue 18, before residue 19). This is the only extracellular N-terminal position possible. Python confirms residue_before=A (pos 18, last of SP), residue_after=E (pos 19, mature N-terminus). Full-length HA-tagged SDC4 construct with HA-tag described as located 'in the N-terminus of the extracellular domain' (L7) and detected by 'antibody against the N-terminal HA-tag' (L5); expressed in SL-29 cells with surface localization confirmed by fluorescence microscopy. RT-qPCR shows no difference in SDC4 gene expression between tagged and untagged constructs (L6).",
